periú Levonta toún aJgiwvtaton thðû 2Rwvmhû
pavpan.</FOREIGN></NOTE>   <HI REND=BOLD>781</HI>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Epistolhv Flauianouð ejpiskovpou Kwnstantinou poúlewû grafeiðsa proúû toún ajrciepivskopon Levonta thðû
presbutevraû Rwvmhû.</FOREIGN></HEAD> <COL N="0744A"></COL> <P COM="0744"><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Twðé aJgiwtavtohgr_é kaiú makariwtavtwé patriú kaiú sulleitourgwðé
Levonti Flauianoúû ejn Kurivwé caivrein.</FOREIGN></P> <P COM="0744"><COL N="0744B"></COL> <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Eujsebeivaû kaiú touð ojrqotomeiðsqai toún lovgon thðû ajlhqeivaû
oujdeún</FOREIGN> <NOTE N="4" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0744" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0744D"></COL> Ms. Ven.,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>protimovteron iJereuðsi Qeouð.</FOREIGN></NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>timiwvteron iJereuðsin, wJû ejpivstasai, qeofilevstate.
Paðsa gavr hJmwðn ejlpiúû kaiú swthriva, kaiú ajntapovdosiû
twðn ejphggelmevnwn ajgaqwðn, ejnteuðqen ejxhvrthtai.
Diav toi touðto, pavnta</FOREIGN> <NOTE N="5" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0744" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0744D"></COL> Mss. Bas. et Ven.,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ponhtevon hJmiðn kaiú ponhtevon.</FOREIGN></NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>poihtevon hJmiðn kaiú ponhtevon,
uJpeúr thðû ajlhqouðû pivstewû, kaiú twðn ejkteqevntwn kaiú
dogmatisqevntwn uJpoú twðn aJgivwn patevrwn, ejf1 wßé te diaú
pantoúû kaiú ejn pantoivaiû peristavsesi pragmavtwn ajkevraia
