adoptassemus, nisi textus Latinus obstaret.
Sequitur paulo post in eodem ms.:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ajll1 oålon eJautoún
ejkevnwsen eijû toú swðsai toún peplanhmevnon aænqrwpon.</FOREIGN>  Lectio
et haec haud nihili facienda. Ad verbum  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejkevnwsen</FOREIGN>  
in marg. edit. Rom. annotatur  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejnevdwken×</FOREIGN>  lectio
quidem optima, et Latino  <HI REND="ITALIC">impendit</HI>  quam maxime respondens,
sed incertum unde eruta.</NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ajiçdivou gennhvsewû ouæte ti ajpemeivwsen,
